new hospitalization numbers show an  alarming jump in the number of children  affected by covet 19 a study in the  journal jama pediatrics finds more than  5 300 children  and teenagers in 22 states were  hospitalized with the disease  between may and november denise valdez  joining us now with  more in today's health watch  well christian we are talking about  multi-system inflammatory syndrome and  we have had a handful of cases here in  nevada and clark county  the symptoms can present really just  like any other virus but it can lead to  some serious complications  which in that case is going to be that  inflammation we've been talking about  now you would never guess that  eight-year-old van fuqua is bouncing  back from a disease that left him  struggling in a hospital bed now his  mother kate got the virus in november so  the entire family quarantined as a  precaution  a month later van was hit with fatigue  first  then a fever of 104 degrees a rash on  his body he had strawberry tongue  and trouble walking now this is  interesting he tested negative for strep  the flu and two covet tests came back  negative  leaving doctors just scrambling to  figure out what was wrong  he had some really scary numbers on his  labs like his heart was  in heart failure his kidneys looked bad  his liver looked bad  so they were really scrambling trying to  figure out you know  which one of these systems is the  culprit and none of them were  it was all an inflammation reaction to  the virus  so the culprit was the cobit-19 virus  and the diagnosis was misc  short for multi-system inflammatory  syndrome now it is relatively rare  but the complication often presents  itself in  in children more states across the  country are now reporting  increases in pediatric cobit  hospitalizations take a look at the map  in utah a 5 000 increase  arizona 4 000 wisconsin south dakota  ohio and minnesota  are all reporting a more than 1 1 000  increase in these cases in kids now  since  may there have been around 1700 cases of  multi-system inflammatory syndrome  and 26 deaths and remember it can pop  up long after cobit is gone children  with misc  may have fever various symptoms things  from including like abdominal pain  vomiting diarrhea neck pain rash and  bloodshot eyes or they're just feeling  really extra tired so something to be  aware of  as we start to slowly now phase out from  the cobit 19.  back to you guys
 

